- Familiarity with OAuth — new to it? Check the [Authentication](https://developer.aircall.io/docs/authentication) overview.
- OAuth credentials — If you haven't received them yet, apply to the [Tech Partner program](https://aircall.io/partners/technology/signup/).

Before diving into the implementation, it's worth understanding what's happening at each stage. The OAuth flow involves three parties: your app, the Aircall Dashboard, and the Aircall API. The goal is to obtain a permanent `access_token` that your app can use to make API calls on behalf of an Aircall customer.

After the Admin approves, Aircall redirects them to your `redirect_uri` with a short-lived code in the query string. This code expires in 10 minutes — exchange it for an `access_token` immediately.
